WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.463 --> 00:00:19.245
Bobby grinned when he arrived at camp on Friday.

2
00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:21.987
All the campers, including Mr.

3
00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:24.649
Dunn, were wearing their tie-dyed T-shirts.

4
00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:27.331
"We look like a team!"

5
00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:28.432
Bobby said.

6
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.541
"Why did you ask us to wear the T-shirts today?"

7
00:00:32.841 --> 00:00:33.842
Bobby asked Mr.

8
00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:39.384
Dunn. "Because today we are going to be a team," Mr.

9
00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:40.064
Dunn said.

10
00:00:40.084 --> 00:00:42.345
"A business team."

11
00:00:42.365 --> 00:00:46.427
"Remember the lemonade we made a few weeks ago?"

12
00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:47.787
Mr. Dunn asked.

13
00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:49.708
"Of course!

14
00:00:50.648 --> 00:00:53.630
It was sooo good," Izzie said.

15
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:58.912
"Bobby said it was good enough to sell," Mr.

16
00:00:58.952 --> 00:00:59.592
Dunn said.

17
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:03.566
"Today we'll try selling it," Mr.

18
00:01:03.627 --> 00:01:04.267
Dunn said.

19
00:01:04.287 --> 00:01:07.150
"We're having a lemonade stand?"

20
00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.391
Nina cried.

21
00:01:08.411 --> 00:01:13.775
"Yep. So we'll need half our team to make the lemonade.

22
00:01:14.896 --> 00:01:18.940
The other half can paint signs and set up the table," said Mr.

23
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.605
Dunn. Izzie, Nina, and Ethan agreed to make the signs.

24
00:01:25.766 --> 00:01:28.228
Bobby and Jason said they would make the lemonade.

25
00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:33.758
"Everyone is going to love this lemonade," Bobby said to Jason.

26
00:01:33.778 --> 00:01:39.801
"We're going to be rich!"

27
00:01:39.881 --> 00:01:41.242
Jason rolled his eyes.

28
00:01:41.262 --> 00:01:45.745
"Um, I don't think we're going to be rich, Bobby.

29
00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:47.946
How much is one cup?

30
00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:50.427
Probably just a few cents."

31
00:01:51.608 --> 00:01:53.029
"No way!"

32
00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:54.089
Bobby said.

33
00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:56.951
"It should be at least two dollars."

34
00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:02.017
The boys spent two hours making pitchers of lemonade.

35
00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:08.460
Then they brought a cooler of ice outside.

36
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:16.483
The girls and Ethan had made huge signs that said: "Sweet Iced Lemonade, Just 25¢."

37
00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:21.485
There were two tables, chairs, a money box, and paper cups.

38
00:02:25.207 --> 00:02:26.407
twenty-five cents?

39
00:02:27.407 --> 00:02:28.568
Is that a joke?"

40
00:02:28.864 --> 00:02:29.705
Bobby cried.

41
00:02:29.725 --> 00:02:32.486
"No," Izzie said.

42
00:02:32.506 --> 00:02:35.588
"It's a fair price to attract customers."

43
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:39.650
And the kids didn't have to wait long for their first customer.

44
00:02:40.811 --> 00:02:43.092
Soon a woman came running toward them!

45
00:02:44.613 --> 00:02:45.273
It was Ms.

46
00:02:45.313 --> 00:02:47.774
Folani! "Hi, everybody.

47
00:02:47.794 --> 00:02:50.616
I was jogging when I saw your sign.

48
00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:54.978
Lemonade sounds great right now," the principal said.

49
00:02:56.119 --> 00:02:57.339
Nina poured her a cup.

50
00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.202
Bobby added the ice cubes.

51
00:03:04.025 --> 00:03:07.028
Ethan put her dollar in the money box and gave her change.

52
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.211
Ms. Folani gulped down her cup.

53
00:03:11.231 --> 00:03:13.393
"This is delicious.

54
00:03:13.533 --> 00:03:16.776
Thanks! See you in September!"

55
00:03:18.077 --> 00:03:19.639
She jogged back down the road.

56
00:03:22.021 --> 00:03:25.464
By the end of the day, there was only one cup of lemonade left.

57
00:03:28.384 --> 00:03:30.906
And the lemonade stand had made $10.00!

58
00:03:30.926 --> 00:03:36.630
"We should have charged more," Bobby grumbled.

59
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.752
"We'll each only get two dollars!"

60
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:45.356
Suddenly a familiar voice said, "It looks like the lemonade stand was a hit!"

61
00:03:46.396 --> 00:03:48.778
It was Allison from Penny's Dog Shelter.

62
00:03:50.279 --> 00:03:51.300
Allison smiled.

63
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.781
"I stopped by to say thank you."

64
00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.563
"Thank you for what?"

65
00:03:56.923 --> 00:03:57.764
Bobby asked.

66
00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.961
Mr. Dunn coughed.

67
00:03:59.981 --> 00:04:04.364
"Actually I haven't told them about the donation yet.

68
00:04:05.405 --> 00:04:07.606
I wanted to make sure we made enough money."

69
00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:11.369
"Donation?" Bobby repeated.

70
00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:14.451
"To Penny's?"

71
00:04:14.831 --> 00:04:16.492
Jason asked excitedly.

72
00:04:16.512 --> 00:04:19.174
"That's such a great idea, Mr.

73
00:04:19.214 --> 00:04:21.316
Dunn!" Mr.

74
00:04:21.376 --> 00:04:22.096
Dunn nodded.

75
00:04:22.116 --> 00:04:27.420
"We can donate the money as long as it's okay with all of you," he said.

76
00:04:28.508 --> 00:04:29.769
Everyone looked at Bobby.

77
00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.651
Bobby smiled at the rest of the team.

78
00:04:33.671 --> 00:04:36.393
"Of course it's okay."

79
00:04:36.973 --> 00:04:37.874
He looked at Mr.

80
00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.436
Dunn. "But we still should have raised the price!"
